    "body": "## Chat03 complete local release rehearsal - independent evidence review\n\n**Review scope:** Codex reports a read-only synthetic full-stack rehearsal on exact Draft PR446 HEAD `0e3f07e7b8a12aa9333e95ca251de84e65bdb9a5`. This reviewer independently verified live GitHub PR ancestry/status, repository sources, and exact-head GitHub Actions; did **not** independently execute Codex's additional local 40-scenario walkthrough or synthetic restore harness. Treat those extra executions as Codex-reported evidence, not separately observed acceptance.\n\n**GitHub facts:** PR440 `b3448587` -> PR441 `6ad90e6` -> PR442 `f1a4592` -> PR443 `c0e6ccb` -> PR444 `bc3687ec` -> PR445 `7cb5bc8` -> PR446 `0e3f07e` all OPEN/DRAFT/UNMERGED, each child's base SHA exactly equal to the parent's HEAD. Current `main` is still `57244500e58d1ee6f0b7f2f5e87cd2e63bb83dcb`, the initial base of PR440, **not diverged**. This main commit is the merged/squashed Chat03A PR438 (`feat(social-combat): add isolated tactical_v1 lifecycle (#438)`), merge date 2026-10-17. The old Notion *Chat03 plan* paragraph saying PR438 Draft/unmerged and Chat03B not implemented is historical/stale; current canonical Notion and exact repo/PRs take precedence. Worker at PR446 imports the existing merged pure tactical lifecycle from `AsyncScene/Web/conflict/tactical-lifecycle.js`. That file explicitly does not load into active browser gameplay runtime: backend/test readiness does not imply a shipped web client.\n\n**Exact-head published CI evidence:** [Private API #40457090075](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40457090075) SUCCESS, isolated local Wrangler/workerd/D1 really applies 0001-0007 and checks trusted admin, A/B commits, reveal, idempotency, reconnect/restart, revoke/replace, concurrent races, AES recovery and expiry; [CAS SQL #40457090267](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40457090267) SUCCESS, 61/61 Python tests and local D1 checks; [Forensics #40457090102](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40457090102) SUCCESS. These runs are **the same runs as the preceding PR446 review**, not a new CI run independently proving all extra rehearsal paths. Codex separately reports local 40 scenario checks, 8 baseline workerd/CAS, 27/27 offline safety, 17/17 policy and disposable restored-D1 fail-closed exercise with no writes or new PR; those were not rerun here.\n\n**Disposition:** `PASS_REPORTED_CHAT03_LOCAL_RELEASE_REHEARSAL_WITH_VERIFIED_EXACT_HEAD_CI` / **NOT** full hosted/private-alpha/browser/Safari/merge acceptance. No blocker in the *reported* local synthetic scenarios, but `Chat03` remains IN_PROGRESS until separately authorized integration and runtime gate.\n\n**Remaining explicit gates:** approved invite/trust model and handling of second device; admin credential custody, distribution and rotation; gameplay identity, data retention/deletion and recovery horizon; validated gameplay D1 keyring/backup restore, fail-closed disable-access operation and no arbitrary privileged capability SQL bypass; reviewed merge strategy for 7 stacked Draft PRs and CI after every target head changes; explicit permission for dedicated staging D1/Worker and authenticated remote synthetic acceptance; connection to actual web client and user-owned Safari/runtime acceptance. Existing telemetry D1 must never be reused as gameplay store. No merges, deployments or Cloudflare mutations are approved by this comment.\n\n**Recommended next concrete step:** decide minimal private-alpha operator policy and document a checkpoint/recovery + merge/staging gate, rather than new migration/test churn. Keep ownership locks, no force push/rebase, and obtain explicit authorization before any merges or hosted actions.",
